'''Money''' ({{Money}}), also known as Beli, is a type of currency used throughout all of Blox Fruits. It is one of the three primary currencies, the others being {{Fragment|Fragments}} and {{Valor|Valor}}.

Money is used to buy [[Fighting Styles]], [[Swords]], [[Guns]], [[Blox Fruits]], [[Accessories]], [[Abilities]], or [[Raids|Raid Chips]]. It is by far the easiest currency to obtain, as it is not only dropped in high amounts, but its obtainment methods are fast and simple. This makes up for the fact that Money prices are significantly higher than other currencies.

The maximum amount of Money that a player can hold is {{Money|1,000,000,000}} and the maximum amount of money admins can hold is {{Money|inf}} (infinite, achievable only through commands).

==Obtainment==
* Defeating [[Enemies]].
* Defeating [[Bosses]], [[Raid Bosses]].
* Completing [[Quests]].
* Collecting [[Chests]] throughout any island.
* Bring any caught [[fish]] to the [[Fisherman]].
* Opening [[Sunken Chest|sunken chest]] by [[fishing]].
* Taking a [[Wanted Poster]] as a [[Marines|Marine]] and then hunting down the wanted [[Pirates|Pirate]] on the poster.
* Defeating a YouTuber who is part of the [[Blox Fruits Star Program]] (or who drops a [[title]] upon defeat).
* Completing [[Sea Events|sea events]].
* Being gifted money from another player.
* Trading for one time money (a player trading you a certain amount of money via a [[Shop|Gamepass]]), though this method is very unlikely to be possible for most.
* Redeeming certain [[codes]].
* Opening [[Fruit Box|Fruit boxes]].
* Spinning from Event [[NPCs]].

Getting the [[2x Money|2x Money Gamepass]] from the [[Shop]] will double the money earned from all the ways of obtainment (except from [[Chests]]).

