==Obtainment Tips== 
* Server-hopping and defeat [[bosses]] (with quest) in public servers.
* Server-hopping and collecting [[Chests]].
* Defeating [[Sea Beast]]s is one of the fastest ways to grind money in [[Third Sea]], as each [[Sea Beast]] gives around {{Money|450,000}} with [[Shop|2x Money Gamepass]].
* Completing "simple" [[Quests]] (e.g. [[Swan Pirate]]s).
* [[Private Servers|Private servers]] can also be efficiently used to earn money through exploitation of their system.
* Due to the way private servers operate, they can be used to spawn [[Chests]] whenever the player shuts down the private server by using <code>/shutdown</code>.
* With this method, the player can set their spawn point at a place with a lot of [[Chests]] (such as the [[Upper Skylands]], the [[Forgotten Island]], or the [[Haunted Castle]]), collect the [[Chests]], use ‘/shutdown’ to shut down the server, and then rejoin to collect the [[Chests]] again.
* Afk farming a [[NPCs|NPC]] with an autoclicker and an [[Elemental]] [[Blox Fruits|Blox Fruit]].
* Doing Player hunter quest gives money but is not a effective way obtaining money as it has a cooldown and is inefficient compared to other methods .

==Notes==
* Buying money is not recommended in the [[First Sea|First]] and [[Second Sea|Second]] Seas, since players can buy more money at the same cost in the [[Third Sea]].
* It is recommended to save up money to buy a Legendary or Mythical [[Blox Fruits|Blox Fruit]] from the [[Blox Fruit Dealer]] as it is easier to obtain those fruits then from finding them or rolling then at the [[Blox Fruit Gacha]].
* These [[Codes]] are seen as troll codes ([[Easter Eggs]]), as they give very little to almost no Money. These codes (except CHANDLER) are dedicated to an admin by the name of "Fudd". 
** "CHANDLER" gives the player {{Money|0}}.
** "Fudd10" gives the player {{Money|1}}.
** "Fudd10_V2" gives the player {{Money|2}}.

